<title>UK: BT says Cellnet managing director Ford quits.</title>
<headline>BT says Cellnet managing director Ford quits.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Telecommunications Plc said on Tuesday that Howard Ford, managing director of its Cellnet mobile phone business, had quit.</p>
<p>BT said Stafford Taylor, managing director of BT's Personal Communications Division, would become more involved in Cellnet's management until a successor was found. Simon Moffat, Cellnet finance director, would act as managing director in the meantime.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
